<style>
  :root {
    color-scheme: dark;
    --bg: #08090a;
    --panel: #0f1113;
    --panel-2: #14171a;
    --line: #272b30;
    --muted: #8e959d;
    --text: #f5f7f9;
    --accent: #b7ff5a;
    --danger: #ff5f6d;
    --danger-soft: rgba(255, 95, 109, .10);
    --code: #0b0d0f;
  }

  * { box-sizing: border-box; }

  body {
    margin: 0;
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 82% 6%, rgba(183, 255, 90, .07), transparent 30rem),
      radial-gradient(circle at 10% 38%, rgba(128, 105, 255, .08), transparent 28rem),
      var(--bg);
    color: var(--text);
    font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
  }

  .rd-shell {
    width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 32px));
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 28px 0 72px;
  }

  .rd-nav {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 20px;
    padding-bottom: 48px;
  }

  .rd-brand {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    color: var(--text);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 760;
    letter-spacing: -.025em;
  }

  .rd-mark {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    border: 1px solid #3a4046;
    font: 700 14px ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
  }

  .rd-chip {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 7px 11px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font: 600 12px ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
  }

  .rd-hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.05fr) minmax(400px, .95fr);
    gap: 64px;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 34px 0 78px;
  }

  .rd-kicker {
    color: var(--accent);
    font: 650 13px ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
    letter-spacing: .04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 14px 0 22px;
    max-width: 760px;
    font-size: clamp(52px, 7vw, 92px);
    line-height: .91;
    letter-spacing: -.065em;
  }

  .rd-lede {
    max-width: 650px;
    margin: 0;
    color: #c4c9cf;
    font-size: clamp(18px, 2vw, 22px);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .rd-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-top: 32px;
  }

  .rd-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-height: 48px;
    padding: 0 18px;
    border: 1px solid #dfe4e9;
    background: #f5f7f9;
    color: #08090a;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 760;
    border-radius: 8px;
  }

  .rd-proof {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, #111417, #0c0e10);
    border-radius: 14px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 28px 90px rgba(0, 0, 0, .34);
  }

  .rd-proof-head {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--muted);
    font: 600 12px ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
  }

  .rd-proof-body { padding: 20px; }

  .rd-block {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    color: var(--danger);
    font: 800 15px ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
  }

  .rd-alert {
    margin-top: 16px;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 95, 109, .34);
    background: var(--danger-soft);
    border-radius: 9px;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  .rd-metric {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    gap: 14px;
    align-items: end;
    margin-top: 24px;
    padding-bottom: 18px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .rd-metric-label {
    color: var(--muted);
    font: 600 12px ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
  }

  .rd-metric-value {
    margin-top: 7px;
    font: 750 30px ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
    letter-spacing: -.04em;
  }

  .rd-delta {
    color: var(--danger);
    font: 700 14px ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
  }

  .rd-finding {
    padding-top: 18px;
    color: #c9ced4;
    font: 13px/1.6 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
  }

  .rd-finding strong { color: var(--text); }

  .rd-return {
    margin: -34px 0 54px;
    padding: 18px 20px;
    border: 1px solid #35402a;
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: rgba(183, 255, 90, .06);
  }

  .rd-return p { margin: 7px 0 0; color: #c7ccd1; }

  .rd-section {
    padding: 72px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .rd-section-title {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    font-size: clamp(34px, 4vw, 52px);
    letter-spacing: -.045em;
  }

  .rd-section-copy {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 0 38px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .rd-steps {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 14px;
  }

  .rd-step {
    min-height: 260px;
    padding: 22px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--panel);
    border-radius: 12px;
  }

  .rd-step-number {
    color: var(--accent);
    font: 700 12px ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
  }

  .rd-step h2 {
    margin: 28px 0 12px;
    font-size: 22px;
    letter-spacing: -.025em;
  }

  .rd-step p {
    margin: 0;
    color: #aeb4bb;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .rd-config {
    position: relative;
    margin-top: 18px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--code);
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .rd-config pre {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 18px;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    color: #d9dee3;
    overflow: auto;
    font: 13px/1.6 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
  }

  .rd-copy {
    margin: 0 18px 18px;
    padding: 8px 11px;
    border: 1px solid #3c4248;
    border-radius: 7px;
    background: #16191c;
    color: var(--text);
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .rd-zero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 18px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .rd-zero-card {
    padding: 22px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--panel);
    border-radius: 12px;
  }

  .rd-zero-card h3 { margin: 0 0 14px; font-size: 18px; }

  .rd-zero-list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    color: #bec4ca;
  }

  .rd-zero-list li::before {
    content: "✓";
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-right: 10px;
  }

  .rd-limit {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .rd-footer {
    padding-top: 30px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: #747c84;
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .rd-hero, .rd-zero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .rd-hero { gap: 42px; }
    .rd-steps { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .rd-step { min-height: auto; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .rd-shell { width: min(100% - 22px, 1180px); }
    .rd-nav { padding-bottom: 22px; }
    .rd-chip { display: none; }
    .rd-hero { padding-top: 24px; }
    h1 { font-size: clamp(48px, 16vw, 70px); }
  }
</style>

<main class="rd-shell">
  <nav class="rd-nav" aria-label="RunDiff">
    <a class="rd-brand" href="/onboarding">
      <span class="rd-mark">R</span>
      <span>RunDiff</span>
    </a>
    <span class="rd-chip">Rails behavioral review</span>
  </nav>

  <section class="rd-hero">
    <div>
      <div class="rd-kicker">Tests passed. Behavior changed.</div>
      <h1>Your first Behavioral Review in three steps.</h1>
      <p class="rd-lede">
        RunDiff runs the same Rails scenario against the exact baseline and candidate revisions,
        captures runtime evidence, and tells you what changed before the change reaches production.
      </p>
      <div class="rd-actions">
        <a class="rd-button" href="<%= @install_url %>">Install RunDiff on GitHub</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <article class="rd-proof" aria-label="Example RunDiff Behavioral Review">
      <div class="rd-proof-head">
        <span>RunDiff / Behavioral Review</span>
        <span>PR #149</span>
      </div>
      <div class="rd-proof-body">
        <div class="rd-block">✕ BLOCK</div>
        <div class="rd-alert">
          <strong>Tests passed, but runtime behavior changed.</strong><br>
          The functional Rails request still succeeds.
        </div>
        <div class="rd-metric">
          <div>
            <div class="rd-metric-label">SQL queries</div>
            <div class="rd-metric-value">17 → 31</div>
          </div>
          <div class="rd-delta">+82.4%</div>
        </div>
        <div class="rd-finding">
          <strong>DATABASE_QUERY_REGRESSION</strong><br>
          Candidate executed 14 additional SQL queries while the functional scenario still passed.
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <% if @post_install_return %>
    <aside class="rd-return">
      <strong>GitHub setup returned here. Continue with your repository.</strong>
      <p>
        Add <code>rundiff.yml</code> in a candidate branch, then open or update a pull request.
        RunDiff will use the signed GitHub webhook and installation-scoped access to decide what it is authorized to execute.
      </p>
    </aside>
  <% end %>

  <section class="rd-section">
    <h2 class="rd-section-title">Install once. Add one small file. Open a PR.</h2>
    <p class="rd-section-copy">
      The first slice is deliberately narrow: a normal Rails endpoint, PostgreSQL or SQLite,
      and an exact baseline-versus-candidate comparison.
    </p>

    <div class="rd-steps">
      <article class="rd-step">
        <div class="rd-step-number">01 / INSTALL</div>
        <h2>Choose repository access</h2>
        <p>
          Install RunDiff on the Rails repository you want to validate. Repository contents are read,
          while Checks and pull-request feedback are used to publish the Behavioral Review.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="rd-step">
        <div class="rd-step-number">02 / DECLARE</div>
        <h2>Add <code>rundiff.yml</code></h2>
        <p>Point the first scenario at a normal Rails endpoint that is safe to replay in the validation environment.</p>
        <div class="rd-config">
          <pre id="rundiff-config"><%= @configuration %></pre>
          <button class="rd-copy" type="button" onclick="navigator.clipboard.writeText(document.getElementById('rundiff-config').innerText)">
            Copy configuration
          </button>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="rd-step">
        <div class="rd-step-number">03 / REVIEW</div>
        <h2>Open or update a PR</h2>
        <p>
          RunDiff checks out the exact base and candidate commits, discovers Rails plus PostgreSQL or SQLite,
          executes the same scenario on both sides, then publishes an <strong>ALLOW</strong>,
          <strong>REVIEW</strong>, or <strong>BLOCK</strong> result.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="rd-section rd-zero">
    <div>
      <div class="rd-kicker">Repository footprint</div>
      <h2 class="rd-section-title">No RunDiff runtime in your app.</h2>
      <p class="rd-section-copy">
        RunDiff owns the comparison machinery. Your repository only declares the scenario.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="rd-zero-card">
      <h3>You do not add</h3>
      <ul class="rd-zero-list">
        <li>RunDiff gem</li>
        <li>GitHub Action</li>
        <li>middleware or initializer</li>
        <li>Docker configuration</li>
        <li>executor configuration</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="rd-section">
    <div class="rd-zero-card">
      <div class="rd-kicker">v0.1 boundary</div>
      <h3>Rails + PostgreSQL or SQLite.</h3>
      <p class="rd-limit">
        Configuration stays declarative. Arbitrary setup commands, shell hooks, customer secrets,
        MySQL, and general-purpose execution hooks are intentionally outside this onboarding slice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer class="rd-footer">
    GitHub may redirect back here with setup query parameters. They only change this page's navigation guidance.
    RunDiff never treats them as proof of installation ownership and never exposes installation-specific data from them.
  </footer>
</main>
